    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 efficiency score stands as our premier play. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and a significant 13% SP skill advantage against the opposing starter, making him the anchor of our offense. Following closely is **Kyle Tucker** (75.20), who maintains elite status despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status, while **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) rounds out the top tier, weaponizing a 19% SP skill advantage to punish the opposing starter\u2019s 5.23 xERA. These selections are heavily influenced by our prioritization of speed and efficiency; **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill** were specifically boosted by \"Slow SP Delivery\" metrics, which provide a latent edge in our scarcity-heavy SB category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Brayan Rocchio** (59.25) on the bench. While his score was respectable, he fell just short of displacing **Drake Baldwin** or **Liam Hicks** because of the specific platoon alignments and order positions of our starters. **Miguel Vargas** also lurked near the cutline with a 55.84 score; despite an elite 0.403 xwOBA, the optimizer favored **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose dynamic platoon advantage (14%) and guaranteed #2 lineup spot offered a more reliable path to run production. \n\nRisks for today center on the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** If these players shift down in the order, their projected efficiency will fluctuate. Additionally, we are monitoring **Josh Lowe** closely; while his base projection is bolstered by a favorable 5% wind-out factor, he faces the toughest opposing arm of the day in T. Bradley (3.74 xERA). Nevertheless, the configuration of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** provides sufficient stability to navigate these uncertainties as we chase critical Roto points.",
